# One origin for the pinned Plane's stock web app and its API, for the browser journeys (issue #45).
#
# The oracle stack (tools/oracle-v1/compose.oracle.yml) is API only: no web, no proxy. Plane's own proxy
# (apps/proxy/Caddyfile.ce in the fork) routes /api/*, /auth/* and /static/* to the API and everything else to the web
# container, which is Caddy with `try_files {path} /index.html` over the built single-page app. This is the same routing for the
# paths a journey uses, in one container: the API for those three prefixes, the built bundle for the rest.
#
# Not routed, as in the Worker that the Thrust leg runs against: /god-mode (admin), /spaces (space) and /live (the collab server).
# They fall through to the app's index.html. A journey that opens the work-item editor's collab provider needs /live (issue #46).
{
	admin off
	auto_https off
}

:8080 {
	@api path /api/* /auth/* /static/*
	handle @api {
		reverse_proxy api:8000
	}

	# The browser's uploads (the project cover, an attachment): the API, with USE_MINIO=1 (compose.ui.yml), signs the URL for this
	# origin with the bucket as the first path segment (AWS_S3_BUCKET_NAME in .env.oracle: `uploads`), and the object store checks the
	# signature against the Host header it is sent. reverse_proxy keeps the Host header it was given, so this works as it does in
	# Plane's own proxy.
	@store path /uploads/*
	handle @store {
		reverse_proxy plane-minio:9000
	}

	handle {
		root * /srv
		try_files {path} /index.html
		file_server
	}
}
